    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0530" n="454" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.00/528</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Curtis to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-12T16:00:00-00:43">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 12, 1916, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s February 7, 4 p.m. Liberian Government desires <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Chester</hi> remain until revolt crushed. I recommend
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Chester</hi> remain at least two weeks after arrival
                    arms and ammunition. Commander <hi rendition="#italic">Chester</hi> concurs.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
